@startuml
title Jarvis --personal-proxy: ask an external LLM by voice, without the voice or the identifying details leaving the machine
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center
skinparam noteFontSize 11
autonumber

actor User
box "LOCAL MACHINE (nothing here touches the network except Ollama on localhost)" #EAF4EA
  participant "Mic / App" as App
  participant "Speech guard\n(silence / noise filter)" as Guard
  participant "Whisper STT\nfaster-whisper, GPU" as STT
  participant "Gemma check\nlocal Ollama\nsample + judge" as Check
  participant "Gemma sanitize\ntext only, reasoning off" as San
  participant "Topics file\n(plain text, local only)" as Topics
  participant "Payload builder\n(single chokepoint)" as Build
  participant "Outbound gate\ndeterministic, blocking" as Gate
  participant "Confirmation\nexchange" as Conf
  participant "Restoration\nGemma + validator" as Rest
  participant "Chat / Journal" as Chat
end box
box "NETWORK (explicit capability: launch flag + configured endpoint)" #FBEAEA
  participant "External LLM\nOpenAI-compatible API" as Ext
end box

== 1. Capture and transcription (audio never leaves the machine) ==
User -> App: asks a question by voice
App -> Guard: audio clip
alt silence or noise
  Guard --> App: drop clip
  note right of Guard: Whisper invents text on noise,\nso the clip never reaches it.\nNothing is sent.
else speech present
  Guard -> STT: clip
  STT --> Check: text + per-word probabilities
end

== 2. Check the transcript against the recording ==
Check -> Check: Gemma hears the clip again,\nweak words marked [?]
Check -> Check: judge lists doubtful fragments
alt call or parse failure
  Check --> San: Whisper text + a doubt (fail safe, never a retry loop, never a send)
else ok
  Check --> San: checked transcript + doubt list
end
note over Check, San
  The doubt list travels with the request to the confirmation step (4);
  it is not recomputed from the sanitized text.
end note

== 3. Sanitize (text only) ==
Topics --> San: sensitive topics
San -> San: replace identifying details\nwith typed placeholders\n<PERSON_1>, <ORG_2> ...
alt malformed or unparseable output
  San --> User: nothing sent (fail closed)
else verdict = refuse (whole topic is sensitive)
  San --> User: refused, reason given, nothing sent
else verdict = send
  San --> Conf: sanitized_text + mapping (placeholder -> original)
end
note over San, Conf: mapping stays local. Originals are never sent.

== 4. Confirmation (only when there is a reason to doubt) ==
alt doubts exist (decided in step 2: the judge listed at least\n[personal_proxy].doubt_min_listed doubts; budget: about 1 request in 4)
  Conf -> Chat: show the WHOLE heard text
  Conf -> User: voice names what to check
  alt clear "yes", spoken or typed
    User --> Conf: yes
  else "no", unclear answer, or timeout
    User --> Conf: no / unclear / silence
    Conf --> User: nothing sent, offer to correct by text or dictate again
  end
else no doubts
  note over Conf: sent without a question (send by default)
end

== 5. Outbound gate (last step before the network) ==
Conf -> Build: sanitized_text only\n(no audio, images, history, memory,\nor --mcp-mode text)
Build -> Gate: complete outbound payload
Gate -> Gate: (a) patterns: email, phone, card+Luhn,\nIBAN, digit runs, key/password shapes, addresses
Gate -> Gate: (b) no original value from mapping\n(exact or stem) appears in payload
Gate -> Gate: (c) no topics-file text appears in payload
alt blocked
  Gate --> User: category + position (never the value), nothing sent
else dry-run enabled
  Gate --> Chat: show exact payload and intermediate state, nothing sent
else passed
  Gate --> Ext: HTTPS request, API key from env var\n(key, payload, response never logged)
  Chat <-- Gate: record "what went out" (equals the real payload)
end

== 6. External answer and local restoration ==
loop streamed chunks
  Ext --> Rest: answer chunks (with placeholders)
  Rest -> Rest: buffer to sentence boundaries
  alt sentence has no placeholder
    Rest --> Chat: pass through, no model call
  else sentence has placeholders
    Rest -> Rest: local Gemma restores originals\nwith correct grammar (Russian cases)
    alt validation passes
      Rest --> Chat: restored sentence
    else validation fails (placeholder left, or value missing)
      Rest --> Chat: plain substitution, marked as rough
    end
  end
end

== 7. Present and record ==
Chat --> User: Text + Voice answer, labeled "external model"
Chat -> Chat: journal: raw voice, heard text, sanitized request,\nverdict, restored answer (external provenance,\nexcluded from automatic retrieval)

note across
  Honest limit: the sanitizer and the gate REDUCE the chance of a leak, they do not prove its absence.
  Quasi-identifiers (harmless facts that together identify someone) are not detectable by either.
  What the external provider does with the cleaned text is outside Jarvis's control.
end note
@enduml
